<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Matheus	    unloading   wheat	    17,471     U.S.</p>
<p>				     gluten meal     5,337</p>
<p>				     gluten feed     8,708</p>
<p>Liberty Wave     arrived     corn	     17,493     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     41,988</p>
<p>Volgobalt 234    arrived     maize grits     3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Yizel Reze 1     arrived     sunflower meal  2,022     Europe</p>
<p>Mohac		14/7	  sunflower meal  1,363     Europe</p>
<p>Atheras	    14/7	  alfalfa	   1,450     Europe</p>
<p>Flag Nicolas     15/7	  corn	     23,524     U.S.</p>
<p>				     barley	    8,400</p>
<p>				     soya meal	 3,000</p>
<p>Peleduy	    15/7	  bran wheat	2,000     Europe</p>
<p>Halilaga	   17/7	  maize grits     2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Don 2		21/7	  wheat	     1,000     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobalt 246    24/7	  barley	    3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobalt 247    25/7	  barley	    2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Zathay	     30/7	  barley	    2,700     Europe</p>
<p>Paragon	    30/7	  wheat	    19,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  13,000</p>
<p>Ganza		10/8	  corn + soya    22,000     U.S.</p>
<p>					pellets +</p>
<p>					sunflower meal</p>
<p>Fany		 15/8	  n/a		40,000     U.S.</p>
</text>
